      "message": "fix: make 'cellforge test-killer' self-contained (its designed fallback path was unreachable)\n\nEach CLI invocation is a fresh process, but main() stored init state only in\nmodule memory (main.state). So 'cellforge test-killer' ALWAYS hit the\n'Initialize first with \"cellforge init\"' guard and exited 1 — running\n'cellforge init' first cannot help, and the self-contained scaffold path\ninside cmd_killer_demo (workbook='killer-demo' + fresh Dispatcher, written for\nexactly this case) was dead code.\n\nFix: pass a blank state to cmd_killer_demo when no dispatcher is live; its\nexisting 'd is None' branch scaffolds the demo. 'cellforge status' keeps its\ngraceful message (fixing init-state persistence is a design decision left to\nthe owner — noted, not smuggled in).\n\nReceipts (Python 3.12.14):\n- before: PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m cellforge test-killer -> exit 1,\n  'Initialize first with \"cellforge init\"'\n- after:  PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m cellforge test-killer -> exit 0,\n  100/100 workers acked, drift 0 ticks, latency 1.05ms, '[OK] PERFECT PAUSE'\n- suite unaffected: python3 run_tests.py -> 42/42 passed, exit 0",
