      "message": "v0.4.1 — Causal-consistency verdict on rewind (R10 Theme T5)\n\nAdds a small but important doctrinal safeguard discovered by the multi-LLM\nAdversary Round 10: when rewinding, check that the witness chain is causally\nlinked — i.e., that replaying tick N will reproduce tick N+1. Without this,\nusers get subtle 'future doesn't match past' bugs after rewind.\n\nNew API:\n- Dispatcher.bind_workbook(wb) — wire dispatcher↔workbook in both dirs\n- Dispatcher.rewind_to(target_tick) now returns a verdict dict:\n    {ok, violations, checks, target_tick, recommended_action, reason}\n  - 'proceed' if no violations\n  - 'warn'   if ≤10% violations\n  - 'block'  if >10% violations (or no ticks/non-causal adjacency)\n  - 'skip'   if no workbook bound (assume causal)\n\nNew Workbook helpers:\n- witnessed_state_hash(tick) — sha256 of all event content_hashes at tick\n- causally_consistent(tick_t, tick_t1) — True if t1 events reference t0 events\n\n5 new tests (42 total, was 37). All pass.\n\nCross-project durable insight (cellforge): Rewind is a trust claim, not a\nstate operation. The user is asking 'will the past I see be the past I\nget if I press play?' — make that claim auditable.",
