      "message": "cellforge v0.3.0: PREDICTING + JEPA stub + JEV verifier\n\nAdversary Round 6-8 prioritized PREDICTING as the third mode after\npause + rewind. With JEPA-style forecasting + uncertainty quantification.\n\nAdded:\n- Mode.PREDICTING (5th mode) — fork ledger, write to PREDICTION_CELLs\n- Dispatcher.enter_predicting(scenarios) / exit_predicting()\n- Dispatcher.active_fork_id — fork metadata\n- PredictionCell — distribution over values (NOT point estimate)\n  - normalized() — sums to 1.0\n  - entropy() — Shannon entropy\n  - to_canonical() — highest-prob value if confidence > threshold\n- JEPAPredictor (stub) — linear extrapolation + Gaussian uncertainty\n- JEVVerifier (stub) — cosine-style score vs observed value\n  - should_promote() — boolean gate based on agreement_threshold\n\n6 new tests (31/31 total):\n- predicting_creates_fork_id\n- predicting_exits_to_paused\n- prediction_cell_normalized\n- prediction_cell_entropy\n- jepa_predictor_basic\n- jev_verifier_basic\n\nPer Qwen-Max-Thinking Theme 22: predictions are epistemic (distributions),\nnot ontic (point estimates). The stub uses Gaussian bins with std growing\nwith horizon.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Mavis <noreply@anthropic.com>",
